<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">reinforced-harness</ansi> (tailoring recipe)

A chest-worn harness of layered, cured leather stitched over webbing and
doubled straps, every seam sewn twice until nothing in it can flex. It
was built to answer a load rather than absorb it -- bolt a cradle to its
frame and the leather holds true, no creak, no give, no shifting weight
settling wrong across the shoulders. Simple work, honestly done, meant
to disappear under whatever it is asked to carry.

